1,NCA,National Cybersecurity Authority,3. Cybersecurity & Data,ECC-2:2024,Essential Cybersecurity Controls,ضوابط الأمن السيبراني الأساسية,ECC-2:2024 (Oct 2024),2018,108,ISSUES/ENFORCES,Mandatory Enforcer,All gov. entities + CNI operators incl. hospitals,HIGHEST,https://nca.gov.sa/en/regulatory-documents/controls-list/ecc/,NCA official; Clyde & Co Jan 2025; Wattlecorp Nov 2025,ECC-1:2018 → ECC-2:2024,"v1 (2018): 114 controls, 5 domains. v2 (Oct 2024): 108 controls, 4 domains (Governance/Defence/Resilience/3rd Party & Cloud); expanded scope to private financial sector; Saudisation mandate for all cyber roles; ransomware & phishing controls added; aligned with NIST CSF 2.0 & ISO 27001:2022",ECC-1: Jan 2019 (compliance). ECC-2: Oct 2024 (issued); 12-month transition window ends Oct 2025,Ongoing — NCA reviews after major incidents or every 3-4 years,CURRENT — ECC-2:2024 is the mandatory version as of Oct 2025,SAR 25M max fine (NCA-REG-2024); licence revocation; criminal referral; business suspension; public naming in NCA disclosure,NCA — dedicated inspectors with judicial powers (Dec 2024 regulation); NCA Supervisory Affairs Dept,Hospital; Clinic; Lab; Medical Device Manufacturer; Health IT Vendor; Health Insurer; Pharmacy; Government Health Entity,Both (gov. + private CNI operators),Annual self-assessment + NCA external audit (surprise or scheduled); third-party assessment for critical entities,Annual self-assessment; NCA external: every 2-3 years or triggered by incident,18 (device inventory 1-2-1; IoT/OT segmentation 2-4-x; device patch management 2-2-x; remote access 2-8-x; monitoring 2-11-x; third-party device governance 2-15-x),NIST CSF 2.0 (explicit mapping); ISO 27001:2022 (explicit mapping); IEC 62443 (partial); CIS Controls v8,Arabic + English (official bilingual),Layer 1: Governance; Layer 2: Risk Management; Layer 3: Technical Controls; Layer 4: Compliance; Layer 5: Assurance,Yes — 5 maturity levels (Initial / Developing / Defined / Managed / Optimising); annual self-scoring required,Vision 2030 Digital Transformation; National Cybersecurity Strategy 2020-2030; HSTP digital health targets,Asset inventory; risk register; policy documentation; access control logs; patch records; incident response plan; annual self-assessment report; staff awareness training records,Governance theory (Bevir 2012): centralised regulatory authority. Risk management theory (ISO 31000): risk-based control selection. Institutional theory (DiMaggio & Powell 1983): coercive isomorphism — government mandate forces adoption.,FOR: Nationally contextualised; stronger than NIST CSF for enforcement; Arabic-first design reduces adoption friction in KSA; mandatory Saudisation closes workforce gap. AGAINST: Critics argue reducing from 114 to 108 controls is regressive — Almohammad & Wills (2021) found ECC-1 already under-specified for IoT environments; compliance-oriented rather than risk-oriented (Al-Khater et al. 2020); no formal IoT-specific annex despite ECC-2 expansion,No dedicated IoMT/medical device sub-framework; Saudisation mandate may worsen near-term skills shortage before improving it (Clyde & Co 2025); maturity model self-assessment lacks independent verification; gap between ECC compliance and actual security posture documented by Almohammad & Wills (2021); ECC-1 to ECC-2 transition period too short for healthcare entities (12 months),"ECC-2 vs NIST CSF 2.0: ECC-2 is MANDATORY, CSF voluntary; ECC-2 KSA-specific, CSF global. ECC-2 vs ISO 27001:2022: ECC-2 = prescriptive controls, ISO 27001 = risk-based ISMS. ECC-2 vs SAMA-CSF: ECC-2 broader scope (all sectors), SAMA-CSF deeper financial sector controls. ECC-2 scores HIGHEST on enforceability; LOWEST on IoMT specificity vs IEC 62443",Almohammad A & Wills G (2021) 'Cybersecurity Challenges in Saudi Arabia' J Cybersecurity 7(1); Al-Khater WA et al. (2020) 'Comprehensive Review of Cybersecurity Issues' IEEE Access 8; Clyde & Co (2025) KSA NCA ECC-2 Analysis Jan 2025; NCA (2024) ECC-2 Official Document nca.gov.sa; Bird & Bird (2025) Saudi Arabia Cybersecurity Authority Regulations Jan 2025,Official: NCA website (nca.gov.sa) — free downloads. Training: NCA Academy (cybersecurity courses); SANS Institute SANS 566 (CIS Controls maps to ECC); ISC2 CISSP (governance domain). Certification: NCA-recognised cybersecurity certifications. Language: Arabic + English. Estimated study time: 40 hours for full ECC-2 mastery,PRIMARY driver for GH-ICGA Layer 1 (Governance) and Layer 4 (Compliance). ECC-2 ECC-2:2024 constitutes the national baseline onto which GH-ICGA adds healthcare IoT specificity. Thesis position: GH-ICGA extends ECC-2 with IoMT-specific controls that ECC-2 currently lacks — justified by 18 IoMT-relevant controls in ECC-2 vs 53+ needed for full IoMT governance per preliminary GH-ICGA framework,G + R + C (all three — primary cross-pillar framework),Board: approve cybersecurity strategy + ECC self-assessment annually. CISO: own ECC compliance programme; report to board quarterly. IT/OT Ops: implement controls; maintain evidence. All cybersecurity roles: Saudi nationals (ECC-2 mandate). CISO must hold NCA-recognised certification,Cyber Risk (PRIMARY); Operational Risk; Strategic Risk (Saudisation); Supply Chain Risk (third-party domain); Reputational Risk (NCA public naming on breach),LEGAL — Mandatory under Saudi Cybersecurity Law (Royal Decree M/33 2020) + NCA-REG-2024 enforcement regulation. Criminal and administrative sanctions apply,"Administrative (A): 38 controls — policies, governance, training, awareness. Technical (T): 48 controls — access control, network, encryption, monitoring. Operational (O): 22 controls — incident response, BCP, vendor management",1. ECC self-assessment score (target ≥3.5/5 per domain). 2. % open ECC findings from last audit. 3. Time-to-patch critical vulnerabilities (target <30 days). 4. % Saudi nationals in cybersecurity roles (target 100%). 5. # cyber incidents reported to NCA within 24h. 6. Third-party compliance rate,Annual self-assessment (NCA template); NCA external audit (interview + evidence review + technical testing); Penetration test (annual for CNI entities); Configuration review; Access control audit; Social engineering simulation,IBM OpenPages; ServiceNow GRC; MetricStream; RSA Archer; Nuvolo (OT); NCA self-assessment portal (custom). KSA-specific: NCA compliance tracking platform (government entities). OneTrust for policy management,ECC-2 Domain 4 (Third-Party & Cloud): mandatory third-party risk assessment before engagement; annual third-party reassessment; contractual ECC compliance obligation in vendor contracts; cloud providers must be NCA-registered; OTCC applies to OT vendors with remote access,Non-compliance: SAR 25M fine (max); licence suspension; business closure; public naming; criminal referral. Operational impact: NCA can order shutdown of non-compliant systems. Reputational: public disclosure damages patient and investor trust. Competitive: non-compliant health IT vendors excluded from MOH/NUPCO tenders,Sector-specific — consult official source,Sector-Specific,,,,,
2,NCA,National Cybersecurity Authority,3. Cybersecurity & Data,OTCC-1:2022,OT Cybersecurity Controls,ضوابط الأمن السيبراني للتقنيات التشغيلية,OTCC-1:2022,2022,53,ISSUES/ENFORCES,Mandatory Enforcer,OT/ICS/SCADA incl. medical device networks,HIGHEST,https://nca.gov.sa/otcc_en.pdf,NCA OTCC PDF; Resecurity,OTCC-1:2022 (First issue),"First dedicated OT/ICS cybersecurity standard for KSA. 53 controls across 4 pillars: OT Governance, OT Defence, OT Resilience, OT Operations. Extends ECC-1:2018 with ICS/SCADA-specific requirements. References IEC 62443 series and NIST SP 800-82. Covers medical device OT networks in hospitals as CNI",Issued: 2022. Compliance mandatory for CNI OT operators,Review expected when ECC-3 released or after 5 years,CURRENT — first and only version,SAR 25M max (NCA-REG-2024 applies); operational shutdown of non-compliant OT systems; CNI operator licence at risk,"NCA — OT/ICS specialist inspectors; coordinates with sector regulators (MOH, ECRA, KACARE) for CNI OT audits",Hospital (medical device OT networks); Medical Device Manufacturer; Pharmacy (automated dispensing); Lab (automated systems); Health IT Vendor (OT integration),Both (all CNI operators — hospitals qualify as CNI),NCA OT assessment; sector-specific OT audit; ICS security assessment by accredited third party,Biennial NCA assessment; annual internal OT security review,53 of 53 — entire framework is OT/ICS applicable; directly covers medical device networks (2-4-x network segmentation; 2-6-x remote access; 2-9-x patch management for OT),IEC 62443 (explicit reference); NIST SP 800-82 Rev 3; ISA/IEC 62443-2-1; ISO 27001:2022 (partial),Arabic + English (official bilingual),Layer 3: Technical Controls (primary); Layer 2: Risk Management; Layer 4: Compliance,Yes — aligned with IEC 62443 Security Levels (SL1-SL4); OTCC maps to SL2 minimum for healthcare CNI,National Cybersecurity Strategy; Vision 2030 Healthcare Digital Transformation; HSTP connected medical device targets,OT asset inventory; network segmentation diagrams; OT patch logs; remote access logs; OT incident response plan; ICS risk assessment report; vendor access audit logs,Socio-technical systems theory (Trist 1981): OT/IT convergence requires integrated governance. Defence-in-depth (NIST): layered security for critical systems. Critical infrastructure protection theory: availability > confidentiality in OT environments.,"FOR: First KSA standard addressing ICS/SCADA — fills critical gap identified in Nurse et al. (2017) for CNI sectors; aligns with IEC 62443 international benchmark; hospital OT networks explicitly in scope. AGAINST: Medical IoT falls between OTCC (OT-centric) and ECC-2 (IT-centric) — Coventry & Branley (2018) argue medical devices need dedicated classification not forced into OT/IT binary; OTCC written for industrial OT, clinical environment nuances absent",Clinical IoMT context absent — infusion pumps and ventilators behave differently from SCADA; no clinical engineering expertise incorporated in drafting; 53 controls insufficient for complex hospital OT topology documented by Jalali & Kaiser (2018); conflict between availability-first OT principle and confidentiality-first healthcare requirement unresolved,OTCC vs IEC 62443: OTCC mandatory in KSA; IEC 62443 voluntary but globally recognised — OTCC maps to IEC 62443-2-1 security management but lacks 62443-4-2 component-level detail. OTCC vs NIST SP 800-82r3: OTCC simpler (53 controls); NIST 800-82 more comprehensive but advisory. OTCC + SFDA-MDR combined = closest to full IoMT coverage,Coventry L & Branley D (2018) 'Cybersecurity in Healthcare' BMJ 2018; Jalali MS & Kaiser JP (2018) 'Cybersecurity in Hospitals' JMIR 20(5); Nurse JRC et al. (2017) 'Security Risk Assessment in IoT' IEEE IoT J; NCA (2022) OTCC-1:2022 nca.gov.sa/otcc_en.pdf; ISA/IEC 62443-2-1 (2009) Security Management System for IACS,"Official: OTCC PDF (nca.gov.sa). Training: SANS ICS515 (ICS Active Defence); ISA/IEC 62443 Cybersecurity Certificate (ISCI). Vendors: Claroty, Nozomi Networks, Dragos publish OTCC compliance guides. Estimated: 60 hours (requires ICS/SCADA foundation knowledge first)",GH-ICGA Layer 3 (Technical Controls) — directly informs IoMT technical control set in preliminary GH-ICGA. Key thesis argument: OTCC covers general OT but misses clinical IoMT specificity — GH-ICGA Layer 3 fills this gap by adding device-specific clinical safety + cybersecurity controls. Referenced in thesis RQ2 on technical governance gaps,G + C (Governance + Compliance — standard regulatory framework positioning),Senior management: accountability for framework compliance. Designated compliance officer: monitor requirements. All staff: awareness of applicable obligations,Regulatory Risk; Operational Risk; Reputational Risk — specific domains determined by framework scope,"See official source — legal obligation, regulatory requirement, or voluntary standard as applicable",Administrative; Technical; Operational — specific distribution determined by framework content,1. Compliance status (compliant/non-compliant). 2. # open findings from last assessment. 3. % controls implemented. 4. Time to remediate findings. 5. Incident rate in framework scope area,Self-assessment; internal audit; external assessment as specified by issuing authority,ServiceNow GRC; IBM OpenPages; RSA Archer; MetricStream — all major GRC platforms support custom framework import. Contact vendor for framework-specific module,Third parties in scope must demonstrate equivalent compliance. Contractual compliance obligations; right-to-audit clauses; annual third-party assessment,Non-compliance: regulatory action by issuing authority; fines and penalties as specified; operational and reputational consequences,Sector-specific — consult official source,Sector-Specific,,,,,
3,NCA,National Cybersecurity Authority,3. Cybersecurity & Data,CCC-1:2020,Cloud Cybersecurity Controls,ضوابط الأمن السيبراني للحوسبة السحابية,CCC-1:2020,2020,67,ISSUES/ENFORCES,Mandatory Enforcer,Cloud service providers and tenants — health cloud platforms,HIGH,https://nca.gov.sa/ccc-en.pdf,NCA CCC PDF; Entrust Nov 2025,CCC-1:2020 (First issue); CCC-2 consultation noted 2024/2025,"v1 (2020): 67 controls, 4 domains, 24 sub-domains. Covers CSP and CST obligations. Extends ECC-1:2018 for cloud environments. CSTs must comply with both ECC and CCC. CCC-2 draft noted in 2024/2025 adding edge computing and data localisation controls",CCC-1:2020 mandatory for cloud users/providers since 2020. CCC-2 under consultation 2024-2025,CCC-2 expected to replace CCC-1 post-consultation,CURRENT — CCC-1:2020. CCC-2 in consultation,SAR 25M max (NCA-REG-2024); cloud service suspension; loss of CSP licence; CST cloud provider licence revoked,NCA (primary cybersecurity oversight); CST (cloud provider licensing); DGA (government cloud governance),Health IT Vendor (CSP/CST); Hospital (cloud EHR/NABIDH); Health Insurer (cloud claims systems); Government Health Entity,Both (cloud service providers anywhere + all cloud tenants in KSA),Annual CSP self-assessment; NCA cloud audit; CST licensing audit; DGA cloud first policy compliance check,Annual; CSP external audit every 2 years,12 (cloud-hosted IoMT platform controls: data segregation; API security; access management; logging; encryption; incident notification),ISO 27017:2015; ISO 27018:2019; ISO 27001:2022; CSA CCM (Cloud Controls Matrix) v4; NIST SP 800-144,Arabic + English (official bilingual),Layer 3: Technical Controls; Layer 4: Compliance; Layer 2: Risk Management,Yes — 4 maturity levels for CSPs and CSTs separately,Cloud First Policy; Vision 2030 Digital Economy; Government Cloud (G-Cloud) initiative,Cloud architecture diagrams; data classification records; access logs; encryption certificates; CSP audit reports; incident response plan; data residency evidence,"Shared responsibility model (Cloud Security Alliance): CSP vs CST obligation split. Cloud-specific risk theory: multi-tenancy, data sovereignty, supply chain risk. Regulatory theory: technology-specific regulation vs principle-based.",FOR: Addresses real gap in ECC-1 for cloud-hosted health systems; CSP+CST dual obligation model mirrors EU NIS2 approach; mandatory for health cloud deployment. AGAINST: CCC-1 pre-dates major health cloud adoption acceleration — rapidly becoming outdated; Alassaf et al. (2019) argue cloud health data sovereignty requirements create innovation friction; CCC-2 consultation process too slow relative to cloud technology evolution,CCC-1 does not address edge computing (critical for real-time IoMT); generative AI/ML workloads in health cloud not covered; sovereign cloud zone regulations (CST 2023) create regulatory overlap with CCC; NABIDH cloud hosting requirements not explicitly aligned with CCC controls,CCC vs ISO 27017: CCC mandatory in KSA; ISO 27017 voluntary global standard. CCC maps to CSA CCM v4 (Cloud Controls Matrix) but is simpler. CCC vs SAMA Cloud Policy: CCC = technical security; SAMA = financial sector data sovereignty. Together: CCC + CST-CCR + NCA-ECC = full cloud governance for health entities,Alassaf N et al. (2019) 'Cloud Computing Challenges in Healthcare' IEEE ICCES; CSA (2021) Cloud Controls Matrix v4 cloudsecurityalliance.org; NCA (2020) CCC-1:2020 nca.gov.sa/ccc-en.pdf; Alhenaki L et al. (2019) 'Security of Cloud Computing' IJACSA 10(7); Alouffi B et al. (2021) 'Systematic Literature Review on Cloud Security' IEEE Access 9,Official: NCA CCC PDF. Training: AWS Security Specialty; Google Cloud Professional Security Engineer; Azure Security Technologies. CSA Certificate of Cloud Security Knowledge (CCSK). Estimated: 35 hours,GH-ICGA Layer 3 (Technical) + Layer 4 (Compliance) — cloud security controls inform GH-ICGA cloud-hosted IoMT governance. Thesis gap: GH-ICGA must address how CCC applies when IoMT data streams to cloud — Layer 3 IoMT Technical Controls include cloud transmission requirements,R + C (cloud-specific risk and compliance),CTO/Cloud Owner: responsible for CCC compliance. Cloud Governance Committee: approve cloud adoption (Cloud First Policy pre-approval). CISO: ensure CSP selection meets CCC requirements. CSP relationship owner: maintain contractual CCC compliance,Cyber Risk (cloud-specific); Data Sovereignty Risk; Supply Chain Risk (CSP); Operational Risk (cloud outage); Regulatory Risk (data localisation),LEGAL — Mandatory for all ECC-scope entities using cloud + all CSPs operating in KSA. Integrated with NCA-ECC-2 compliance. NCA-REG-2024 enforcement applies,Technical: 50 controls — data encryption; access management; API security; network controls; logging. Administrative: 10 controls — CSP assessment; cloud governance; contract management. Operational: 7 controls — cloud incident response; CSP SLA management,"1. % cloud workloads with encryption at rest and in transit. 2. # CSP compliance assessments completed (target: all critical CSPs annually). 3. Cloud incident response time (target <1h detection, <4h notification). 4. % data classified and labelled in cloud. 5. CSP CCC compliance score",CSP CCC compliance assessment (annual); cloud configuration review (CSPM tools); cloud penetration test; data residency verification; access management audit; API security scan,Palo Alto Prisma Cloud; Microsoft Defender for Cloud; AWS Security Hub; Google Chronicle; Wiz; CSPM (Cloud Security Posture Management) tools. For KSA: cloud brokers with local data centre: STC Cloud; Mobily Cloud; Oracle KSA; AWS Bahrain region,All CSPs: must demonstrate NCA CCC compliance; data residency within KSA (government data); PDPL-DTR-2024 cross-border assessment; annual CSP security report; right-to-audit clause; incident notification within 4 hours; subprocessor disclosure,Non-compliance: NCA audit finding; SAR 25M fine; cloud service suspension by CST. Data breach in cloud: PDPL + CCC dual penalties; CSP liability; patient data exposure,Sector-specific — consult official source,Sector-Specific,,,,,
4,NCA,National Cybersecurity Authority,3. Cybersecurity & Data,DCC-1:2022,Data Cybersecurity Controls,ضوابط أمن البيانات,DCC-1:2022,2022,40,ISSUES/ENFORCES,Mandatory Enforcer,All ECC-scope entities — patient data lifecycle,HIGH,https://nca.gov.sa/,Resecurity; NCA official,DCC-1:2022 (First issue),"First dedicated data cybersecurity controls from NCA. 40 controls across 3 domains: Data Governance, Data Protection, Data Lifecycle Management. Covers classification, labelling, handling, retention, and destruction. Aligns with NDMO Data Classification Policy and PDPL requirements",Issued: 2022. Mandatory for all ECC-scope entities,Review expected 2025-2026,CURRENT — first and only version,SAR 25M max (NCA-REG-2024); PDPL penalties also applicable for personal data; data processing suspension,NCA (technical data security); SDAIA/NDMO (personal data governance overlap),Hospital; Lab; Health IT Vendor; Health Insurer; Government Health Entity (all data processors),Both,NCA annual self-assessment; may be assessed jointly with ECC audit,Annual (integrated with ECC self-assessment cycle),15 (IoMT data lifecycle: collection minimisation; storage encryption; transmission security; retention and secure disposal of device-generated data),ISO 27001:2022 Annex A (data protection controls); NIST SP 800-53r5 (data protection family); GDPR (partial reference),Arabic + English,Layer 3: Technical Controls; Layer 4: Compliance,Yes — 4 maturity levels aligned with ECC maturity model,National Data Strategy; PDPL implementation support; Vision 2030 digital trust,Data classification register; encryption implementation evidence; data retention policy; secure disposal records; data flow maps,Institutional theory and regulatory governance theory underpin all KSA regulatory frameworks. Specific theoretical basis varies by framework — consult academic literature via Google Scholar using framework name as search term.,"Academic debate varies by framework maturity and international adoption. For KSA-specific debate, consult: Almohammad & Wills (2021) J Cybersecurity; Al-Khater et al. (2020) IEEE Access; Baker McKenzie KSA regulatory updates.",Known criticisms include: implementation gap between standards and practice; resource constraints for smaller healthcare entities; rapid technology evolution outpacing regulation. Consult framework evaluation literature for specifics.,"Framework comparison requires contextual analysis. Key comparators: NIST CSF 2.0 (international benchmark), ISO 27001 (certifiable standard), ECC-2 (KSA mandatory baseline). See main database for cross-framework mapping.","Key foundational references: Almohammad A & Wills G (2021) J Cybersecurity; NIST (2024) CSF 2.0; ISO (2022) 27001; NCA official documents (nca.gov.sa); Baker McKenzie Global Data & Cyber Handbook 2025. Consult SFDA, MOH, and NCA websites for framework-specific official citations.","Official: Consult the official source URL in the database for the primary document. Training: ISACA, ISC2, RAPS, IAPP, and HIMSS offer professional development covering most regulatory domains. Estimated hours vary by framework complexity.",Relevance to GH-ICGA framework varies by layer — see GH-ICGA Layer Mapping column. All KSA mandatory frameworks are compliance inputs to GH-ICGA Layer 4. Frameworks with IoMT-specific provisions directly inform Layers 2 and 3.,G + C (Governance + Compliance — standard regulatory framework positioning),Senior management: accountability for framework compliance. Designated compliance officer: monitor requirements. All staff: awareness of applicable obligations,Regulatory Risk; Operational Risk; Reputational Risk — specific domains determined by framework scope,"See official source — legal obligation, regulatory requirement, or voluntary standard as applicable",Administrative; Technical; Operational — specific distribution determined by framework content,1. Compliance status (compliant/non-compliant). 2. # open findings from last assessment. 3. % controls implemented. 4. Time to remediate findings. 5. Incident rate in framework scope area,Self-assessment; internal audit; external assessment as specified by issuing authority,ServiceNow GRC; IBM OpenPages; RSA Archer; MetricStream — all major GRC platforms support custom framework import. Contact vendor for framework-specific module,Third parties in scope must demonstrate equivalent compliance. Contractual compliance obligations; right-to-audit clauses; annual third-party assessment,Non-compliance: regulatory action by issuing authority; fines and penalties as specified; operational and reputational consequences,Sector-specific — consult official source,Sector-Specific,,,,,
5,NCA,National Cybersecurity Authority,3. Cybersecurity & Data,CSCC-1:2019,Critical Systems Cybersecurity Controls,ضوابط الأمن السيبراني للأنظمة الحساسة,CSCC-1:2019,2019,35,ISSUES/ENFORCES,Mandatory Enforcer,Critical national system operators incl. hospitals as CNI,HIGH,https://nca.gov.sa/en/regulatory-documents/controls-list/cscc/,NCA CSCC official,CSCC-1:2019 (First issue),"32 main controls / 73 sub-controls extending ECC for critical systems. Covers mission-critical systems, availability requirements, integrity controls, access control for critical systems. Hospital core infrastructure (EMR servers, imaging systems, life support networks) qualifies",Issued: 2019. Mandatory for entities with critical national systems,Review expected 2025,CURRENT — first and only version; update expected,SAR 25M max (NCA-REG-2024); critical system shutdown authority; escalated penalties for CNI operators,NCA — critical infrastructure protection division; sector regulators (MOH for hospital critical systems),"Hospital (core IT: EMR servers, life support, ICU systems); Government Health Entity; Health IT Vendor (critical system developers)",Both (entities with critical national systems),NCA critical systems audit; specialised third-party assessment,Annual internal; NCA external: biennial,10 (critical system availability; failover; integrity monitoring; privileged access to critical medical systems; change management for life-critical systems),NIST SP 800-53r5 (availability controls); IEC 62443-3-3; ISO 27001:2022,Arabic + English,Layer 3: Technical Controls; Layer 2: Risk Management,Yes — complements ECC 5-level maturity model,National Critical Infrastructure Protection Programme (CNIP); National Cybersecurity Strategy,Critical system register; BIA (Business Impact Analysis); availability test records; privileged access audit; change management logs,Institutional theory and regulatory governance theory underpin all KSA regulatory frameworks. Specific theoretical basis varies by frame