6,NCA,National Cybersecurity Authority,3. Cybersecurity & Data,TCC-1:2021,Telework Cybersecurity Controls,ضوابط الأمن السيبراني للعمل عن بعد,TCC-1:2021,2021,28,ISSUES/ENFORCES,Mandatory Enforcer,All ECC-scope entities with remote workers — telehealth clinicians,MODERATE,https://nca.gov.sa/en/regulatory-documents/controls-list/tcc/,NCA TCC official,TCC-1:2021 (First issue),"21 main controls / 42 sub-controls across 3 domains: Telework Governance, Telework Security, Telework Monitoring. Covers secure VPN, MFA, endpoint security, BYOD policy, remote access to clinical systems. Healthcare application: telehealth clinicians accessing patient records remotely",Issued: 2021. Mandatory for ECC-scope entities with remote workers,Review expected 2025-2026,CURRENT — first and only version,SAR 25M max (NCA-REG-2024); may be assessed as ECC non-compliance,NCA — assessed as part of ECC compliance audit,Hospital; Clinic; Health IT Vendor; Health Insurer; Government Health Entity (all entities with remote workers),Both,Annual self-assessment (integrated with ECC); spot check during NCA audit,Annual,5 (secure remote access to clinical systems; remote device management; VPN requirements for IoMT monitoring platforms),NIST SP 800-114; ISO 27001:2022; CIS Benchmark for remote access,Arabic + English,Layer 3: Technical Controls,Aligned with ECC 5-level model,National Telework Programme; Healthcare Digital Transformation (telehealth staff),VPN configuration evidence; remote access policy; endpoint security records; MFA implementation evidence; remote worker awareness training records,Institutional theory and regulatory governance theory underpin all KSA regulatory frameworks. Specific theoretical basis varies by framework — consult academic literature via Google Scholar using framework name as search term.,"Academic debate varies by framework maturity and international adoption. For KSA-specific debate, consult: Almohammad & Wills (2021) J Cybersecurity; Al-Khater et al. (2020) IEEE Acce