11,NCA,National Cybersecurity Authority,3. Cybersecurity & Data,NCA-REG-2024,NCA Regulatory Framework (Enforcement & Penalties),لائحة الهيئة الوطنية للأمن السيبراني,Dec 2024,2024,N/A,ISSUES/ENFORCES,Mandatory Enforcer,All entities subject to any NCA framework — fines up to SAR 25M,HIGHEST,https://www.twobirds.com/en/insights/2025/,Bird & Bird Jan 2025; Clyde & Co Jan 2025,"First enforcement regulation — Dec 21, 2024","First dedicated NCA enforcement mechanism. Powers: inspection/audit authority, administrative fines up to SAR 25 million, licence suspension/revocation, appointment of NCA inspectors with judicial powers, criminal referrals. Covers all NCA frameworks (ECC, OTCC, CCC, DCC, CSCC, TCC). Significant shift from guidance to enforceable compliance","Issued: Dec 21, 2024. In force immediately",Ongoing enforcement,CURRENT — first enforcement regulation,This IS the penalty framework — SAR 25M max; imprisonment via criminal referral; business suspension; public naming; appeals process defined,NCA — Director General of Supervisory Affairs; NCA Inspectors (appointed Dec 2024 with judicial powers),All healthcare entities subject to any NCA framework,Both,NCA-initiated inspections; complaint-triggered; incident-triggered; scheduled sector reviews,As determined by NCA risk-based approach,"N/A — enforcement mechanism, not technical controls",EU NIS2 Directive (enforcement model reference); Singapore CSA Cybersecurity Act (penalty benchmarking),Arabic (primary); English unofficial translation,Layer 4: Compliance; Layer 5: Assurance,No maturity model — binary compliance/non-compliance,National Cybersecurity Strategy (enforcement pillar),N/A — this is the enforcement regulation; entities must produce evidence of compliance with underlying NCA frameworks,Regulatory enforcement theory (Ayres & Braithwaite 1992): responsive regulation pyramid — persuasion → warning → penalty → criminal referral. Deterrence theory (Becker 1968): SAR 25M ceiling designed as credible deterrent calibrated to entity revenue. Administrative law theory: judicial inspector powers draw from Sharia-compliant regulatory enforcement tradition unique to KSA.,"FOR: First NCA-specific enforcement mechanism closes the 'paper tiger' critique of ECC-1 era; SAR 25M cap is proportionate compared to EU NIS2 (€10M/2% revenue); criminal referral authority adds personal accountability for executives. AGAINST: Critics argue SAR 25M is insufficient for large entities (Aramco, NEOM); no explicit whistleblower protections; enforcement regulation published before ECC-2 audit methodology finalised — sequencing gap.",Criticisms: (1) Enforcement regulation lacks graduated penalty schedule — inspectors have full discretion between SAR 0 and SAR 25M with no guidance; (2) Criminal referral pathway undefined — no precedent case law; (3) No appeal mechanism specified for disputed findings; (4) Saudisation mandate in ECC-2 creates workforce bottleneck for compliance — not enough qualified Saudi cyber professionals yet; (5) Arabic-only official text creates interpretation challenges for international organisations operating in KSA.,"Compared to: EU NIS2 penalties (€10M/2% revenue — higher cap, turnover-linked); UK NIS Regulations (£17M max); Singapore Cybersecurity Act (S$100K — much lower); UAE NESA (case-by-case). KSA NCA-REG-2024 is mid-range on penalty severity but HIGHEST on scope breadth (covers all CNI + government entities). Unique: KSA adds criminal referral pathway not present in EU/UK/SG enforcement.",Ayres & Braithwaite (1992) Responsive Regulation; Bird & Bird (2025) KSA Cybersecurity Enforcement Guide; Clyde & Co (2025) NCA Regulatory Analysis; Al-Qahtani (2024) Administrative Enforcement in Saudi Law; NCA Official Gazette Publication (2024).,"Official: Consult the official source URL in the database for the primary document. Training: ISACA, ISC2, RAPS, IAPP, and HIMSS offer professional development covering most regulatory domains. Estimated hours vary by framework complexity.",GH-ICGA positions NCA-REG-2024 as the ENFORCEMENT ENABLER layer — transforms the entire NCA framework stack from advisory to legally binding. Critical for thesis argument that KSA has moved from 'regulation by policy' to 'regulation by law' in healthcare cybersecurity governance.,G + C (Governance + Compliance — standard regulatory framework positioning),Senior management: accountability for framework compliance. Designated compliance officer: monitor requirements. All staff: awareness of applicable obligations,Regulatory Risk; Operational Risk; Reputational Risk — specific domains determined by framework scope,"See official source — legal obligation, regulatory requirement, or voluntary standard as applicable",Administrative; Technical; Operational — specific distribution determined by framework content,1. Compliance status (compliant/non-compliant). 2. # open findings from last assessment. 3. % controls implemented. 4. Time to remediate findings. 5. Incident rate in framework scope area,Self-assessment; internal audit; external assessment as specified by issuing authority,ServiceNow GRC; IBM OpenPages; RSA Archer; MetricStream — all major GRC platforms support custom framework import. Contact vendor for framework-specific module,Third parties in scope must demonstrate equivalent compliance. Contractual compliance obligations; right-to-audit clauses; annual third-party assessment,Non-compliance: regulatory action by issuing authority; fines and penalties as specified; operational and reputational consequences,ALL 17 SECTORS — all NCA framework subjects,YES — ALL SECTORS,,,,,
