62,SCFHS,Saudi Commission for Health Specialties,2. Healthcare & Life Sciences,NCA-ECC-2:2024,Essential Cybersecurity Controls,ضوابط الأمن السيبراني الأساسية,ECC-2:2024,2018,108,MUST COMPLY WITH,Mandatory Complier,SCFHS as government entity,MODERATE,https://nca.gov.sa/,NCA ECC scope,See official source for version history,Framework issued by the relevant authority. Version details available on the official website referenced in the source URL column. The framework has been updated periodically since first issuance.,See official source,Updated as needed by the issuing authority,CURRENT — consult official source for latest version,Penalties defined by issuing authority; consult official source. NCA ECC-2 penalties apply if relevant,Issuing authority and/or designated inspection department,As specified in framework scope — consult official document,Both (unless specified otherwise in official document),As defined by issuing authority,As defined by issuing authority,To be determined from framework text — see official source,See framework preamble for international standard references,Arabic (primary in KSA); English may be available,Mapped to relevant GH-ICGA layer — requires manual assessment,See official framework for maturity model details,Aligned with relevant Vision 2030 programme — see framework context,As specified in framework compliance requirements,Institutional theory and regulatory governance theory underpin all KSA regulatory frameworks. Specific theoretical basis varies by framework — consult academic literature via Google Scholar using framework name as search term.,"Academic debate varies by framework maturity and international adoption. For KSA-specific debate, consult: Almohammad & Wills (2021) J Cybersecurity; Al-Khater et al. (2020) IEEE Access; Baker McKenzie KSA regulatory updates.",Known criticisms include: implementation gap between standards and practice; resource constraints for smaller healthcare entities; rapid technology evolution outpacing 