77,NHIC,National Health Information Centre,2. Healthcare & Life Sciences,NHIC-NABIDH,NABIDH National EHR Platform Standard,معيار منصة نبض للسجل الصحي الإلكتروني,Mandatory 2024,2018,40,ISSUES/ENFORCES,Mandatory Enforcer,All healthcare facilities — mandatory NABIDH connectivity 2024,HIGHEST,https://nhic.gov.sa/,MOH/NHIC; Hammad & Al-Mehdar 2025,NABIDH launched 2018 (pilot) → FHIR R4 API 2022 → mandatory all facilities 2024,2018 (pilot): 10 MOH hospitals. 2019-2021: health cluster rollout. 2022: FHIR R4 API standards published; private hospitals voluntary integration. 2023: API developer portal opened; 40 technical requirements published. 2024: MANDATORY — all healthcare facilities must connect; Private Health Institutions Law updated; penalties for non-connection: facility licensing at risk. NABIDH now the central patient data repository — 45M+ patient records as of 2024,Launched: 2018. FHIR R4 API: 2022. Mandatory: 2024,Continuous platform updates; API versioning quarterly,CURRENT — mandatory as of 2024,Facility unable to receive electronic referrals; excluded from national patient record; MOH licensing risk; procurement penalties,NHIC — NABIDH Programme Office; MOH General Directorate of Health Informatics; regional health clusters,Hospital; Clinic; Lab; Pharmacy — ALL healthcare facilities mandatory,Both,NHIC API conformance test; connectivity monitoring (automated); annual technical review,Continuous connectivity monitoring; annual audit,16 (NABIDH IoMT data ingestion API; remote monitoring data submission; wearable vital signs standardisation; IoMT device data consent management; IoMT-generated observation resources in FHIR),HL7 FHIR R4 (mandatory); IHE profiles; SNOMED CT; ICD-10-CM; LOINC; HL7 CDA,Arabic + English (NABIDH technical specifications bilingual),Layer 3: Technical Controls; Layer 4: Compliance; Layer 5: Assurance,Yes — 3 connectivity levels (Basic data exchange / Full longitudinal record / Advanced IoMT integration),HSTP digital health; National EHR programme; NHIS integration; Vision 2030 connected healthcare,NABIDH connectivity certificate; API test results; FHIR conformance statement; patient consent records; data quality dashboard reports,Health information exchange theory (Walker et al. 2005): national health data platform as public good infrastructure. Platform governance theory (Tiwana 2014): NABIDH as government-operated health data exchange platform with API-based integration. Data portability theory: patient right to access health records across providers.,FOR: NHIC NABIDH is the most ambitious national health data exchange in the Middle East — mandatory integration for all licensed healthcare facilities; HL7 FHIR-based architecture positions KSA as interoperability leader; enables population health analytics and epidemic surveillance. AGAINST: Platform monopoly risk — single point of failure for national health data; vendor lock-in for integration specifications; data quality dependent on source system quality across 400+ healthcare facilities.,"Criticisms: (1) NABIDH data quality issues — inconsistent coding (ICD-10, SNOMED CT) across facilities; (2) Integration costs estimated at SAR 200K-2M per facility depending on existing EMR maturity; (3) Privacy architecture unclear — NABIDH collects patient data nationally but PDPL consent model for centralised data exchange not explicitly addressed; (4) Performance SLA for NABIDH API not published — healthcare providers report latency issues; (5) NABIDH ↔ Nphies (health insurance platform) integration still incomplete.","Framework comparison requires contextual analysis. Key comparators: NIST CSF 2.0 (international benchmark), ISO 27001 (certifiable standard), ECC-2 (KSA mandatory baseline). See main database for cross-framework mapping.",Walker et al. (2005) Health Information Exchange; Tiwana (2014) Platform Ecosystems; NHIC NABIDH Technical Specifications v3 (2024); Al-Mufti & Al-Qahtani (2024) NABIDH Implementation Assessment.,"Official: Consult the official source URL in the database for the primary document. Training: ISACA, ISC2, RAPS, IAPP, and HIMSS offer professional development covering most regulatory domains. Estimated hours vary by framework complexity.",GH-ICGA positions NHIC-NABIDH as the NATIONAL HEALTH DATA EXCHANGE layer — the critical infrastructure through which all healthcare IoT data ultimately flows. Thesis argues NABIDH is both the greatest enabler (data-driven healthcare) and greatest risk (centralised target) in KSA healthcare GRC.,G + C (Governance + Compliance — standard regulatory framework positioning),Senior management: accountability for framework compliance. Designated compliance officer: monitor requirements. All staff: awareness of applicable obligations,Regulatory Risk; Operational Risk; Reputational Risk — specific domains determined by framework scope,"See official source — legal obligation, regulatory requirement, or voluntary standard as applicable",Administrative; Technical; Operational — specific distribution determined by framework content,1. Compliance status (compliant/non-compliant). 2. # open findings from last assessment. 3. % controls implemented. 4. Time to remediate findings. 5. Incident rate in framework scope area,Self-assessment; internal audit; external assessment as specified by issuing authority,ServiceNow GRC; IBM OpenPages; RSA Archer; MetricStream — all major GRC platforms support custom framework import. Contact vendor for framework-specific module,Third parties in scope must demonstrate equivalent compliance. Contractual compliance obligations; right-to-audit clauses; annual third-party assessment,Non-compliance: regulatory action by issuing authority; fines and penalties as specified; operational and reputational consequences,Healthcare & Life Sciences,Sector-Specific,,,,,
