79,NHIC,National Health Information Centre,2. Healthcare & Life Sciences,NHIC-INTEROP,Health IT Interoperability Framework (FHIR-based),إطار التشغيل البيني لتقنية المعلومات الصحية,2022,2020,25,ISSUES/ENFORCES,Mandatory Enforcer,Health IT vendors and hospital systems — FHIR API compliance,HIGHEST,https://nhic.gov.sa/,NHIC official,See official source for version history,Framework issued by the relevant authority. Version details available on the official website referenced in the source URL column. The framework has been updated periodically since first issuance.,See official source,Updated as needed by the issuing authority,CURRENT — consult official source for latest version,Penalties defined by issuing authority; consult official source. NCA ECC-2 penalties apply if relevant,Issuing authority and/or designated inspection department,As specified in framework scope — consult official document,Both (unless specified otherwise in official document),As defined by issuing authority,As defined by issuing authority,To be determined from framework text — see official source,See framework preamble for international standard references,Arabic (primary in KSA); English may be available,Mapped to relevant GH-ICGA layer — requires manual assessment,See official framework for maturity model details,Aligned with relevant Vision 2030 programme — see framework context,As specified in framework compliance requirements,"Interoperability theory: syntactic, semantic, and organisational levels of health data exchange (Benson & Grieve 2021). Standards governance theory: mandated standards (HL7 FHIR, ICD-10, SNOMED CT) as enablers of semantic interoperability. Network effect theory: interoperability value increases exponentially with participant count.",FOR: NHIC interoperability standards mandate HL7 FHIR R4 — globally current standard; include specific IoMT data exchange profiles for connected medical devices; Arabic clinical terminology mappings enable local-language interoperability. AGAINST: FHIR profile specifications for KSA are still evolving — frequent version changes create integration instability; no certification programme for FHIR-compliant systems — compliance is self-declared.,"Criticisms: (1) No NHIC FHIR certification or testing programme — unlike US ONC Health IT Certification; (2) IoMT device data exchange profiles (IEEE 11073-FHIR mapping) not yet included in NHIC specifications; (3) Arabic clinical terminology (ICD-10 AR, SNOMED CT AR) coverage incomplete for specialist domains; (4) No explicit security requirements within interoperability standards — defers entirely to NCA ECC-2.","Framework comparison requires contextual analysis. Key comparators: NIST CSF 2.0 (international benchmark), ISO 27001 (certifiable standard), ECC-2 (KSA mandatory baseline). See main database for cross-framework mapping.",Benson & Grieve (2021) Principles of Health Interoperability; HL7 FHIR R4 Specification (2024); NHIC Interoperability Standards (2024); IHE Integration Profiles.,"Official: Consult the official source URL in the database for the primary document. Training: ISACA, ISC2, RAPS, IAPP, and HIMSS offer professional development covering most regulatory domains. Estimated hours vary by framework complexity.",Relevance to GH-ICGA framework varies by layer — see GH-ICGA Layer Mapping column. All KSA mandatory frameworks are compliance inputs to GH-ICGA Layer 4. Frameworks with IoMT-specific provisions directly inform Layers 2 and 3.,G + C (Governance + Compliance — standard regulatory framework positioning),Senior management: accountability for framework compliance. Designated compliance officer: monitor requirements. All staff: awareness of applicable obligations,Regulatory Risk; Operational Risk; Reputational Risk — specific domains determined by framework scope,"See official source — legal obligation, regulatory requirement, or voluntary standard as applicable",Administrative; Technical; Operational — specific distribution determined by framework content,1. Compliance status (compliant/non-compliant). 2. # open findings from last assessment. 3. % controls implemented. 4. Time to remediate findings. 5. Incident rate in framework scope area,Self-assessment; internal audit; external assessment as specified by issuing authority,ServiceNow GRC; IBM OpenPages; RSA Archer; MetricStream — all major GRC platforms support custom framework import. Contact vendor for framework-specific module,Third parties in scope must demonstrate equivalent compliance. Contractual compliance obligations; right-to-audit clauses; annual third-party assessment,Non-compliance: regulatory action by issuing authority; fines and penalties as specified; operational and reputational consequences,Sector-specific — consult official source,Sector-Specific,,,,,
