121,MHRSD,Ministry Human Resources & Social Dev.,1. Ministries,MHRSD-NITAQAT,Saudisation / Nitaqat System,نطاقات,Annual update,2011,N/A,ISSUES/ENFORCES,Mandatory Enforcer,All private sector employers — cyber roles must be Saudi (NCA ECC-2),HIGH,https://www.hrsd.gov.sa/en,MHRSD official; Clyde & Co Jan 2025,Launched 2011 → multiple updates; ECC-2 cybersecurity Saudisation 2024,"Nitaqat (Saudisation): quota system by company size and sector. Healthcare sector: tiered quotas for physicians, nurses, pharmacists, admin staff. 2024 critical update — NCA ECC-2 mandates ALL cybersecurity positions in ECC-scope entities (including hospitals) must be filled by Saudi nationals. Colours: Platinum (>>=quota) / Green (meets) / Yellow (below) / Red (significantly below). Non-compliant companies face: work visa bans, government service restrictions",Launched: 2011. Annual sector-specific updates. ECC-2 cyber Saudisation: Oct 2024,Annual quota updates; cybersecurity Saudisation deadline: Oct 2025,CURRENT — 2024 version with cyber Saudisation mandate,Red zone: work visa ban; government services suspension; business licence at risk; SAR fines per violation; forced nationalisation order,MHRSD — Labour Inspection Department; Qiwa platform automated monitoring; NCA enforces cyber Saudisation via NCA-REG-2024,Hospital; Clinic; Health IT Vendor; Medical Device Manufacturer; Health Insurer; Pharmacy (private sector employers),Private sector only (Saudisation does not formally apply to government),Qiwa platform continuous monitoring; MHRSD labour inspection; NCA cyber workforce compliance audit,Continuous (Qiwa real-time); quarterly colour rating update,3 (cybersecurity roles for IoMT system administrators; biomedical engineer Saudisation; clinical informatics staff),"ILO standards (employment); regional Saudisation comparators (Emiratisation UAE, Omanisation)",Arabic (primary); English guidance on Qiwa portal,Layer 1: Governance,Colour-coded zone system: Platinum / Green / Yellow / Red — updated quarterly,Vision 2030 Saudisation targets; National Labour Market Strategy; NCA SCyWF cybersecurity workforce development,GOSI registration records; Qiwa Nitaqat colour certificate; Saudi employee contracts; NCA ECC-2 cybersecurity role audit; SCFHS licence for Saudi clinical professionals,Institutional theory and regulatory governance theory underpin all KSA regulatory frameworks. Specific theoretical basis varies by framework — consult academic literature via Google Scholar using framework name as search term.,"Academic debate varies by framework maturity and international adoption. For KSA-specific debate, consult: Almohammad & Wills (2021) J Cybersecurity; Al-Khater et al. (2020) IEEE Access; Baker McKenzie KSA regulatory updates.",Known criticisms include: implementation gap between standards and practice; resource constraints for smaller healthcare entities; rapid technology evolution outpacing regulation. Consult framework evaluation literature for specifics.,"Framework comparison requires contextual analysis. Key comparators: NIST CSF 2.0 (international benchmark), ISO 27001 (certifiable standard), ECC-2 (KSA mandatory baseline). See main database for cross-framework mapping.","Key foundational references: Almohammad A & Wills G (2021) J Cybersecurity; NIST (2024) CSF 2.0; ISO (2022) 27001; NCA official documents (nca.gov.sa); Baker McKenzie Global Data & Cyber Handbook 2025. Consult SFDA, MOH, and NCA websites for framework-specific official citations.","Official: Consult the official source URL in the database for the primary document. Training: ISACA, ISC2, RAPS, IAPP, and HIMSS offer professional development covering most regulatory domains. Estimated hours vary by framework complexity.",Relevance to GH-ICGA framework varies by layer — see GH-ICGA Layer Mapping column. All KSA mandatory frameworks are compliance inputs to GH-ICGA Layer 4. Frameworks with IoMT-specific provisions directly inform Layers 2 and 3.,G + C (workforce governance + regulatory compliance),CEO: organisation's Nitaqat colour rating — executive accountability. HR Director: Saudisation strategy and execution. CISO: ensure cybersecurity roles are Saudi nationals per NCA ECC-2. Department Heads: headcount planning within Saudisation quotas,Regulatory Risk; Operational Risk (recruitment constraints); Strategic Risk (Saudisation in skilled roles); Reputational Risk (Red zone = public knowledge),LEGAL — Labour Law (RD M/51 2005 as amended). Enforced via Qiwa platform automated monitoring. Red zone: visa ban = operational inability to hire expats,Administrative (A): workforce planning; GOSI registration; Qiwa compliance; training programmes. Operational (O): recruitment pipeline for Saudi nationals; transfer of knowledge programmes,1. Nitaqat colour rating (target: Green or Platinum). 2. Saudisation percentage vs sector quota. 3. % cybersecurity roles filled by Saudi nationals (target 100% per NCA ECC-2). 4. Saudi employee retention rate (target >85%). 5. Time-to-fill Saudi national vacancies (target <60 days),Qiwa platform continuous automated monitoring; GOSI contribution verification; MHRSD labour inspection (random); NCA audit (cybersecurity role Saudisation),Qiwa portal (mandatory — MHRSD); GOSI self-service portal; SAP SuccessFactors (Saudisation tracking module); Oracle HCM; Workday HR (Saudisation reporting); HRDF Hadaf portal,Contractors: must meet Saudisation requirements independently; staffing agencies: Green zone minimum required; cybersecurity service providers: must employ Saudi nationals in roles working for client (NCA ECC-2 mandate),Red zone: work visa ban (cannot hire expats) = operational impact on healthcare services heavily reliant on expat clinical staff; government service suspension; reputational damage (MHRSD public Nitaqat ratings); CCHI contract implications for private insurers,ALL 17 SECTORS (private sector) — all private employers,YES — ALL SECTORS,,,,,
