orcement; data subject rights fulfilment process; cross-border transfer review,1. # data subject rights requests fulfilled on time (target: 100% within 30 days). 2. # data breaches notified to SDAIA within 72h (target: 100%). 3. % staff completed privacy training (target: 100%). 4. # DPIAs completed for high-risk processing activities. 5. Data retention compliance rate (% records within policy). 6. % third-party processors with DPA agreements,Annual DPIA review; data mapping audit (controller record validation); consent record audit; breach response simulation (tabletop); access control review for personal data systems; third-party processor audit; SDAIA compliance self-assessment,OneTrust (market leader for PDPL); TrustArc; Nymity; DataGrail; Varonis (data discovery); Microsoft Purview (data classification). SDAIA National Data Governance Platform for registration. Arabic-capable tools preferred,All third-party data processors must have Data Processing Agreement (DPA). Processors must demonstrate equivalent PDPL compliance. Cross-border transfers require adequacy assessment or appropriate safeguards. Sub-processor disclosure mandatory. Annual processor risk assessment required,Non-compliance: SAR 5M administrative fine; criminal prosecution for sensitive data breach; SDAIA investigation; mandatory breach public disclosure. Business disruption: SDAIA can order processing suspension. Reputational: patient trust damage. Market: EU adequate protection status depends on PDPL enforcement credibility,ALL 17 SECTORS — any entity processing personal data,YES — ALL SECTORS,,,,,
