s 2 and 3.,G + C (Governance + Compliance — standard regulatory framework positioning),Senior management: accountability for framework compliance. Designated compliance officer: monitor requirements. All staff: awareness of applicable obligations,Regulatory Risk; Operational Risk; Reputational Risk — specific domains determined by framework scope,"See official source — legal obligation, regulatory requirement, or voluntary standard as applicable",Administrative; Technical; Operational — specific distribution determined by framework content,1. Compliance status (compliant/non-compliant). 2. # open findings from last assessment. 3. % controls implemented. 4. Time to remediate findings. 5. Incident rate in framework scope area,Self-assessment; internal audit; external assessment as specified by issuing authority,ServiceNow GRC; IBM OpenPages; RSA Archer; MetricStream — all major GRC platforms support custom framework import. Contact vendor for framework-specific module,Third parties in scope must demonstrate equivalent compliance. Contractual compliance obligations; right-to-audit clauses; annual third-party assessment,Non-compliance: regulatory action by issuing authority; fines and penalties as specified; operational and reputational consequences,Healthcare & Life Sciences,Sector-Specific,,,,,
