446,BHHC,Baha Health Cluster,17. Regional Health Clusters,MOH-PR,Patient Rights Charter,ميثاق حقوق المريض,2019,2012,45,MUST COMPLY WITH,Mandatory Complier,Baha Health Cluster facilities,HIGH,https://www.moh.gov.sa/en/,MOH official,First Charter ~2012 → updated 2019,"45 rights and obligations. Key provisions: informed consent (including electronic consent for telemedicine), right to access medical records (digital access through NABIDH patient portal), right to privacy of health information, right to refuse treatment, right to second opinion. 2019 update added digital health rights (right to data portability from health apps)",First: ~2012. Updated: 2019,Review 2024-2025 expected to add AI/algorithmic transparency rights,CURRENT — 2019 version,Penalties defined by issuing authority; consult official source. NCA ECC-2 penalties apply if relevant,Issuing authority and/or designated inspection department,As specified in framework scope — consult official document,Both (unless specified otherwise in official document),As defined by issuing authority,As defined by issuing authority,To be determined from framework text — see official source,See framework preamble for international standard references,Arabic (primary in KSA); English may be available,Mapped to relevant GH-ICGA layer — requires manual assessment,See official framework for maturity model details,Aligned with relevant Vision 2030 programme — see framework context,As specified in framework compliance requirements,Institutional theory and regulatory governance theory underpin all KSA regulatory frameworks. Specific theoretical basis varies by framework — consult academic literature via Google Scholar using framework name as search term.,"Academic debate varies by framework maturity and international adoption. For KSA-specific debate, consult: Almohammad & Wills (2021) J Cybersecurity; Al-Khater et al. (2020) IEEE Access; Baker McKenzie KSA regulatory updates.",Known criticisms include: implementation gap between