CBAHI-HAS-H,Hospital Accreditation Standards (5th Ed.),1st Ed 2008 → 2nd Ed 2011 → 3rd Ed 2014 → 4th Ed 2017 → 5th Ed 2021,"5th Edition (2021, current): 298 standards across domains including Patient and Family Rights, Patient Assessment, Care of Patients, Patient Safety, Medication Management, Infection Prevention, Facility Management, Staff Qualifications, Quality Improvement, Governance, HIT (Health Information Technology). HIT standards require EMR, NABIDH connectivity, access control, audit trails, downtime procedures. IoMT requirements added in 5th Ed: medical device integration standards, alarm management policy. Benchmarked against JCI standards",1st Ed: 2008. 2nd: 2011. 3rd: 2014. 4th: 2017. 5th: 2021,6th Edition expected 2025-2026,CURRENT — 5th Edition 2021
CBAHI-HAS-LAB,Laboratory Accreditation Standards,1st Ed 2012 → 2nd Ed 2019,"2nd Edition (2019): 80 standards for clinical laboratories. Aligned with ISO 15189 and ISO 17025. Covers pre-analytical, analytical, post-analytical phases; quality management; proficiency testing; biosafety; result reporting (including critical values); LIS integration requirements for NABIDH",1st: 2012. 2nd: 2019,3rd Edition expected 2024,CURRENT — 2nd Edition 2019
CBAHI-HAS-LTC,Long-Term Care Standards,1st Ed 2018 (First issue),"First dedicated long-term care accreditation standards in KSA. 90 standards covering care planning, activities of daily living, dementia care, palliative care, medication management, safety (falls, pressure injuries), infection control, staff competencies. IoMT: remote monitoring requirements for high-dependency residents; fall detection sensor standards",1st Ed: 2018,2nd Edition expected 2024-2025,CURRENT — 1st Edition 2018
CBAHI-HAS-PHC,Primary Health Care Accreditation Standards,1st Ed 2010 → 2nd Ed 2015 → 3rd Ed 2020,"3rd Edition (2020): 145 standards for PHC centres. Covers chronic disease management (diabetes, hypertension), preventive services, family medicine, mental health services, pharmacy, infection control, records management. IoMT: remote patient monitoring for chronic disease management; telemedicine integration requirements aligned with MOH-TELE",1st: 2010. 2nd: 2015. 3rd: 2020,4th Edition expected 2024-2025,CURRENT — 3rd Edition 2020
CCC-1:2020,Cloud Cybersecurity Controls,CCC-1:2020 (First issue); CCC-2 consultation noted 2024/2025,"v1 (2020): 67 controls, 4 domains, 24 sub-domains. Covers CSP and CST obligations. Extends ECC-1:2018 for cloud environments. CSTs must comply with both ECC and CCC. CCC-2 draft noted in 2024/2025 adding edge computing and data localisation controls",CCC-1:2020 mandatory for cloud users/providers since 2020. CCC-2 under consultation 2024-2025,CCC-2 expected to replace CCC-1 post-consultation,CURRENT — CCC-1:2020. CCC-2 in consultation
CCHI-DCS,Digital Claims Processing Standards,Mandatory digital claims 2024-2025 (First issue),"End-to-end digital claims processing requirement. Phase 1 (2024): e-submission mandatory for major insurers (>50,000 covered lives). Phase 2 (2025): all insurers. Requirements: CCHI-standard JSON/XML claims format; 48-hour claims acknowledgement; 15-day clean claims payment; NABIDH integration for clinical data validation; real-time claims status visibility; audit trail for all claim decisions",Phase 1: 2024. Phase 2: 2025,Annual update,CURRENT — phased rollout 2024-2025
CCHI-HIR,Cooperative Health Insurance Law & Regulations,"Royal Decree M/10 1999 → major updates 2006, 2012, 2020, 2024","1999 (establishment): mandatory health insurance for expat workers. 2006: expanded to all private sector employees. 2012: new insurance products approved. 2020: mental health coverage mandated (first time). 2024: major update — chronic disease management coverage expanded; digital health services coverage (telemedicine, remote monitoring reimbursement); mandatory e-prior authorisation; employer penalties for non-compliance strengthened; universal health insurance roadmap integration","Established: 1999. Major updates: 2006, 2012, 2020, 2024",Biennial review; NHI integration updates annually,CURRENT — 2024 version
