CST-DCS,Data Center Services Regulations,Issued 2024 (First dedicated data center regulation),"First dedicated data center services licensing regulation in KSA. Requirements: physical security (CCTV, access control, biometric); redundant power (N+2 minimum); connectivity (multiple ISPs); cooling standards; fire suppression; environmental monitoring; geographic distribution requirements; health data centers must meet highest tier requirements. Aligns with Uptime Institute Tier III/IV standards",Issued: 2024,Review 2026,CURRENT — 2024
CST-DPS,Digital Platform Services Regulations,Issued Oct 2024 (First comprehensive version),"Regulations for digital content platform services (streaming, social media, user-generated content). Covers: platform licensing; content moderation obligations; data localisation; user data protection (aligned with PDPL); transparency reporting; algorithmic accountability. Healthcare application: health information platforms, patient community apps, AI health chatbots as digital content services",Issued: Oct 2024,Review 2026,CURRENT — Oct 2024 version
CST-IOT,IoT Regulatory Framework,IoT Regulatory Framework first ~2019; actively updated,IoT-specific licensing and technical standards. Covers: device type approval (spectrum compliance); data handling obligations for IoT device operators; security requirements for IoT device manufacturers (default password prohibition; firmware update mechanism required; vulnerability disclosure); IoT platform operator licensing. Healthcare application: medical IoT devices sold/deployed in KSA must obtain CST type approval in addition to SFDA registration,First: ~2019. Active updates,Under active development; medical IoT sub-framework expected 2025,CURRENT — active updates ongoing
