OSH-REGS,Occupational Safety & Health Regulations,First ~2005 → comprehensive update 2020; sector-specific guides issued,"2005 (first): basic occupational hazard controls. 2020 comprehensive update: aligned with ILO-OSH 2001 and ISO 45001:2018; risk assessment mandatory; OSH committee required (>100 employees); incident reporting system (GOSI coordination); sector-specific guides for healthcare (sharps injury prevention, radiation safety, MRI safety, laser safety). Healthcare OSH committee must include infection control officer and clinical engineer",First: ~2005. Major update: 2020,Next major review 2024-2025,CURRENT — 2020 comprehensive version
OSMACC-1:2021,Social Media Cybersecurity Controls,OSMACC-1:2021 (First issue),"18 controls for official social media account security. Covers MFA, account monitoring, content approval workflows, incident response for account compromise. Healthcare application: hospital official accounts, MOH social media security",Issued: 2021,Review 2025,CURRENT — first and only version
OTCC-1:2022,OT Cybersecurity Controls,OTCC-1:2022 (First issue),"First dedicated OT/ICS cybersecurity standard for KSA. 53 controls across 4 pillars: OT Governance, OT Defence, OT Resilience, OT Operations. Extends ECC-1:2018 with ICS/SCADA-specific requirements. References IEC 62443 series and NIST SP 800-82. Covers medical device OT networks in hospitals as CNI",Issued: 2022. Compliance mandatory for CNI OT operators,Review expected when ECC-3 released or after 5 years,CURRENT — first and only version
PDPL-2021,Personal Data Protection Law,Royal Decree M/19 (16 Sep 2021) → amended Apr 2023,"Original (2021): 19 articles covering consent, data subject rights, controller obligations, sensitive data (health = sensitive), cross-border transfer. Apr 2023 amendment: strengthened enforcement, clarified health data provisions, aligned with PDPL-IR-2023. Grace period for compliance ended Sep 14, 2024. Penalties: up to SAR 5 million fine + 2 years imprisonment for sensitive data breach","Issued: Sep 2021. Amended: Apr 2023. Fully enforceable: Sep 14, 2024",SDAIA reviews annually; amendments expected 2025-2026,CURRENT — fully enforceable since Sep 2024
PDPL-DTR-2024,Data Transfer Regulation (revised),"DTR v1: Sep 7, 2023 → DTR v2 (replacement): Sep 1, 2024","v1 (Sep 2023): Initial data transfer regulation allowing transfers via adequacy, contractual clauses, consent, or necessity. v2 (Sep 1, 2024): Complete replacement. Significant change: removed automatic adequacy for certain jurisdictions; introduced mandatory risk assessment before any cross-border health data transfer; controller accountability strengthened; specific provisions for cloud-hosted patient data transferred to overseas servers","DTR v1: Sep 2023. DTR v2 (replacement): Sep 1, 2024",Annual review by SDAIA; adequacy list publication expected 2025,CURRENT — DTR v2 (Sep 2024)
PDPL-IR-2023,PDPL Implementing Regulations,Issued 7 Sep 2023 (22/2/1445H); multiple ministerial updates to Jun 2025,"89 detailed implementing articles. Key provisions: health data requires explicit consent + necessity justification; DPO mandatory for large-scale health data processors; 72-hour breach notification to SDAIA; cross-border transfer assessment; individual rights (access, correction, deletion, objection); registration obligation for certain controllers. Updates to Jun 2025 clarified breach notification and international transfer rules","Issued: Sep 7, 2023. In force with PDPL: Sep 14, 2024",SDAIA issues ministerial decisions periodically; next major update expected 2025,CURRENT — with amendments to Jun 2025
