SCyWF,Saudi Cybersecurity Workforce Framework,SCyWF v1 2022 → updated 2024 with ECC-2 Saudisation mandate,National taxonomy of cybersecurity roles and competency levels. Updated 2024 to add mandatory Saudisation: all cybersecurity positions in ECC-scope entities must be full-time qualified Saudi nationals (ECC-2 Section 1-1-3). Healthcare CISO and SOC analyst roles affected directly,v1 issued 2022. Saudisation mandate: Oct 2024 (ECC-2). Compliance window: Oct 2025,Annual review with job market changes,CURRENT — updated 2024
SCyber-Edu,Saudi Cybersecurity Higher Education Framework,SCyber-Edu v1 2022 (First issue),"Curriculum framework for university-level cybersecurity programmes. Defines core competencies, elective tracks, lab requirements. Aligned with SCyWF role taxonomy. Supports national pipeline for Saudi cybersecurity professionals required by NCA frameworks",Issued: 2022,Review every 3 years,CURRENT — first version
SDAIA-AI-ADO,AI Adoption Framework,First issue Sep 2024,"AI adoption readiness framework with 5 dimensions: Strategy, Data, Technology, People, Governance. Health entities deploying clinical AI must complete readiness assessment. AI risk tiers defined (medical diagnosis = high risk requiring pre-deployment review). Aligns with Saudi AI Strategy and SFDA AI/ML medical device guidance",Issued: Sep 2024,Annual review,CURRENT — first version
SDAIA-AI-ETH,AI Ethics Principles (2nd Ed.),1st Edition 2019 → 2nd Edition late 2023,"1st Ed (2019): 5 principles (Human-centred, Fairness, Privacy, Reliability, Transparency). 2nd Ed (late 2023): Expanded to address generative AI, hallucination risks, AI in high-stakes decisions (medical diagnosis), human oversight requirements, liability for AI-caused harm. Healthcare AI systems must document ethical review process",1st Ed: 2019. 2nd Ed: late 2023,3rd edition expected 2025-2026 post-GenAI regulatory landscape maturation,CURRENT — 2nd Edition 2023
SDAIA-GENAI,Generative AI Guidelines,Two versions published early 2024: Government employees version + General public version,"Government version: prohibits sharing classified/sensitive data with GenAI tools; requires approved GenAI platforms; human review of AI outputs in official documents. General version: awareness-based, recommends caution with personal health information in GenAI prompts. Healthcare application: clinical staff using AI scribing tools, AI diagnostic aids",Issued: early 2024,Rapid evolution expected; formal regulation anticipated 2025,CURRENT — early 2024 versions
SDAIA-NSDAI,National Strategy for Data & AI,National Strategy for Data & AI 2020-2030 (updated periodically),"6-dimension strategy: Regulation & Policy, Ecosystem & Infrastructure, Data, Talent, Innovation, International. Health data as strategic national asset. Targets: KSA in top 15 globally for AI readiness; national health data platform (NABIDH); AI-enabled diagnosis deployment across MOH facilities by 2030",Launched: 2020. Annual progress reports,Ongoing — 2030 horizon with annual targets,ACTIVE — 2020-2030 strategy
