ZATCA-EINV-P1,E-Invoicing Phase 1 (Generation),"Phase 1 Dec 1, 2021","Generation phase: all VAT-registered taxpayers must generate electronic invoices (standard and simplified) in a structured format (XML/PDF/A-3). Invoices must have UUID, QR code, date, supplier/buyer details, VAT amount. Hospital billing systems, pharmacy POS, medical device invoices all require e-invoice generation. Hardware and software certified by ZATCA required","Mandatory from: Dec 1, 2021",Ongoing; businesses must maintain compliant systems,MANDATORY — Dec 2021
ZATCA-EINV-P2,E-Invoicing Phase 2 (Integration),"Phase 2 rolled out in waves from Jan 1, 2023 onwards (by taxpayer size)","Integration phase: real-time integration of e-invoicing system with ZATCA Fatoora portal. Requirements: ZATCA API connection; cryptographic stamp (ZATCA-issued certificate); UUID generated by ZATCA; clearance model for standard invoices (real-time); reporting model for simplified invoices (24-hour batch). Phased rollout by revenue: largest taxpayers from Jan 2023, rolling to all by 2025. Hospital systems and pharmacy chains in early waves","Phase 2 start: Jan 1, 2023 (wave 1). All taxpayers: 2025",Ongoing rollout,CURRENT — phased rollout Jan 2023-2025
